dialect protocol
protocol stdio.ply.mutations
version 1
schema stdio.ply.op
start op

# 🎫️26/08/10/ARTIFACT-SYSTEM-OVERHAUL-REAL-CODECS-RUNTIME-REUSE-EVOLUTION FG3: real binary op
# frame `protocol::OpBinary::encode_op`/`decode_op` for `PlyMutation` — upgraded this program
# (P2-FG3) from the F6-era `print_op().into_bytes()` text-as-binary shortcut. `PlyMutation` is
# HAND-ROLLED (not `#[derive(dsl::DslOps)]`-able — `PlyValue`/`PlySnapshot`/`PlyElement`/`PlyRow`
# are all `DslField`-unsatisfied, see `../🦀️.rs`'s module doc comment for the real
# `cargo check` citation), so there is no `dsl::variants_binary`-generated frame to forward to
# (unlike gif89a's own sibling protocol file, whose `GifMutation` DOES derive cleanly). Modeled
# by hand instead, same shape as json's own hand-rolled `JsonMutation` frame
# (`📖️grammar-recipe.md` §2.5): `format u8` (`store::pack_rt::OP_BINARY_FORMAT` convention) +
# `tag u8` (the `PlyMutation` variant ordinal, same 0-9 order `print_ply_mutation`'s own match
# uses) as two REAL fixed fields, then the variant's own payload as one opaque trailing `bytes`
# chain — genuinely, fully structured on the Rust side (`../🦀️.rs`'s
# `RealBinaryOpFrame` region, reusing the sibling diff file's `pub(crate)` binary primitives),
# opaque only at THIS protocol-description layer for the same `protocol-prim-ref-recursion`
# reason the sibling diff protocol file documents (`PlyElement`/`PlyRow`/`PlySnapshot`/`PlyValue`
# are all reachable from some variant's own payload).
framing record
header fixed 2
field format u8
field tag u8
chain payload bytes
